            },
            "createdOn": 1756703157,
            "author": {
                "name": "priyair",
                "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                "username": "priyair"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "meta-ibm:\nBut, I think there's a discussion to be had on whether we should put this into meta-phosphor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "Moved the code to meta-phosphor/recipes-connectivity/openssh/openssh_%.bbappend\nas the upstream yocto did not have a change yet where the weak algorithm was going to be removed, hence the change is relevant to meta-phosphor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please fix your S-o-b to match something in the CLA.  This doesn't look like a legal name."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "Please discuss how this was tested.  For example, built the BMC to use openssh server, and ran the `openssh -vv ...` (double verbose) command to connect to the BMC, and verified the supported server MAC algorithms."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-ibm/recipes-connectivity/openssh/openssh_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "The problem I see here is that if we pull a new version of sshd_config from a upstream yocto rebase and it has something new in it, we wont pick it up. Could we just parse the existing line and remove just SHA1 from it if present (vs. hard coding our own MAC_LINE\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-ibm/recipes-connectivity/openssh/openssh_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "I recommend using the technique per the docs under https://man.openbsd.org/sshd_config > \"MACs\":\n> If the specified list begins with a \u2018-\u2019 character, then the specified algorithms (including wildcards) will be removed from the default set....\n\nSo, instead of replacing the \"MACs\" as shown here, change this code to add new lines something like this:\n```\n# Remove deprecated and undesired MACs: \nMACs \"-hmac-sha1*,umac-*\"\n```\n\nAs Andrew mentioned, this has the advantage of being more durable when the underlying config file changes:\n1. This technique will prevail in the face of minor changes to the sshd_config file.\n2. If sshd_config changes to add new MACs, this technique allows those new MACs to be used."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-ibm/recipes-connectivity/openssh/openssh_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "priyair",
                        "email": "priya_irudayaraj@yahoo.co.in",
                        "username": "priyair"
                    },
                    "message": "Added the exclusion of SHA1 and umac64 in meta-phosphor\n  \nReference: https://pages.github.ibm.com/ciso-psg/main/supplemental/acceptable_encryption.html#MACApprovedAlgorithms\n\nTested on target machine using ssh -vv and below server proposal logs excluded the SHA1 and umac-64 Macs\n\n\n======================================================\ndebug2: peer server KEXINIT proposal\n\ndebug2: MACs ctos: umac-128-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,umac-128@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256,hmac-sha2-512\ndebug2: MACs stoc: umac-128-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,umac-128@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256,hmac-sha2-512\n\n\n=============================================="
                }
            ],
